              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "खाऊ (khāū) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from khāduka, \"biting\" (CDIAL 3871). It is built on khād, \"to eat\". CDIAL glosses the Marathi word \"eating\"."
